# nr-exthost-skill-scripts-office: reduced by the wire audit (t19). Already applied: the module lines of mixdog-skill-scripts/src/lib.rs (mixdogd_exec, qc_pages, review_deck, source_extract) and the shipped::run_native proof change.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-cli main.rs, the SkillRun arm (lead hot file)
The process that runs "mixdogd skill-run" must call, once, before skill_run(..):

    mixdog_skill_scripts::source_extract::install_office_engine(Box::new(<engine over the office entry points>))

install_office_engine has no caller in the tree; until it is installed, source-extract on an office file and qc-pages answer "the office engine is not available in this process" (exit 1). The engine implements mixdog_skill_scripts::source_extract::OfficeEngine: call(args, cwd) -> Result<Value, String> (executeOfficeTool: the parsed result text, or the error text) and measure(deck) -> Result<Measured { issues, document }, String> (issues_portable_ooxml + snapshot_portable_ooxml of the deck). The arguments of call are recorded in fixtures/skill-scripts-office/golden.json (observed.office): open {action,path,mode:'portable',snapshotAfter:false} / snapshot {action,session,limit:200,maxChars:100000} / close {action,session,save:false} / render {action,session,pages:[n]}, and open with output:<scratch copy> for qc-pages.

